  "adaptations": [
    "Replace Arduino millis and ESP random with standard C++17 platform functions.",
    "Use the same platform random source for Chess960.",
    "Initialize Zobrist tables with std::call_once to support one AI worker alongside UI-thread rules.",
    "Correct inherited two-knight insufficient-material detection: two knights can legally mate even though they cannot force mate. FIDE Laws articles 5.2.2 and 6.9 govern possible legal mating sequences.",
    "The Zero application coordinate codec appends c for castling so adjacent-king Chess960 castles stay distinct from ordinary king moves in replay saves and LAN messages; PGN remains standard SAN.",
    "Restore upstream display-coordinate directional navigation and independent Space cycling so legal-target arrows follow the shown board orientation."
  ],
  "rules_reference": "https://handbook.fide.com/chapter/E012023"
